From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: clamp raycluster worker scale up to kueue clusterqueue quota

Ray's in-tree autoscaler calculates desired worker counts based purely on application task and actor resource requirements without awareness of Kubernetes scheduling queue limits. In an environment managed by Kueue, uncoordinated scale-up requests periodically exceed ClusterQueue nominal quota and cohort borrowing limits, creating surplus worker pods that remain indefinitely gated or pending, consuming namespace resources and triggering controller thrashing.

Introduce a ScaleGate reconciler guarded by the ScaleGate feature gate that inspects the managing Kueue ClusterQueue, cohort tree, and flavor definitions to dynamically calculate the maximum feasible worker capacity after deducting head pod requests. Clamp spec.workerGroupSpecs[].maxReplicas to this computed ceiling while preserving original configured limits in annotations so maxReplicas can be restored upon quota growth.
---
